{"text": "Black Hills Regional Heart & Vascular Hospital\n\nDISCHARGE SUMMARY\nPatient: RUNNING BEAR, WENDELL K.\n\nMRN: BH-20447193\n\nEncounter: E-90031877\n\nDOB: July 4, 1967\n\nAdmitted: 05/02/2026\n\nDischarged: 05/06/2026\n\nAttending: Soraya Haddad-Ellis, MD, Cardiology (NPI 1555306962)\n\nPrimary care: Tobias Lundquist, PA-C, Pine Ridge Family Health Clinic\n\nClinic phone: 605-555-0126\n\nReason for admission\nMr. Running Bear is a 58-year-old man, an enrolled member of the Oglala Sioux\nTribe, who presented to the emergency department with two hours of substernal\nchest pressure radiating to the left arm while loading hay. Initial troponin was\nelevated and rose on repeat. ECG showed ST depression in the lateral leads.\n\nHospital course\nHe was diagnosed with a non-ST-elevation myocardial infarction. Cardiac\ncatheterization on 05/03/2026 showed a 90 percent lesion of the mid LAD, treated\nwith one drug-eluting stent. Echo showed EF 45 percent. He had no arrhythmia on\ntelemetry. On hospital day two he developed tremor, sweating and agitation\nconsistent with alcohol withdrawal; he reports drinking six to eight beers nightly\nsince his wife's death last winter. He was treated on the withdrawal protocol and\nseen by the addiction medicine team, and he agreed to an outpatient referral. He\nalso has type 2 diabetes, previously untreated, and smokes a pack a day.\n\nResults at discharge\nTest Result\nLDL 162 mg/dL\n\nHbA1c 9.4%\nCreatinine 1.1 mg/dL\n\nDischarge medications\n aspirin 81 mg daily\n ticagrelor 90 mg twice daily for twelve months; do not stop without calling\ncardiology\n atorvastatin 80 mg nightly\n metformin 500 mg twice daily\n naltrexone 50 mg daily, started 05/05/2026\n nicotine patch, 21 mg\n\nFollow-up\n Cardiology clinic, (605) 555-0180, with Dr. Haddad-Ellis on May 20, 2026 at\n10:30\n Mr. Lundquist within one week for diabetes teaching\n Cardiac rehabilitation referral sent; the nearest program is in Rapid City,\nabout ninety minutes from his home near Kyle, SD\n No driving for one week; no lifting over ten pounds for five days\n\nContact and coverage\nHis sister, Charlene Running Bear, will stay with him for two weeks and can be\nreached at 605 555 0162. Coverage is through the Indian Health Service\npurchased/referred care program, authorization no. PRC-26-0041882, with\nMedicaid secondary (ID SD-774019336). Estimated patient balance: $0.00.\n\nDictated by S. Haddad-Ellis, MD, on 05/06/2026 at 14:12. Electronically signed.", "kind": "PDF", "detail": "2 pages · 376 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Running Bear, Wendell K.", "Soraya Haddad-Ellis", "Tobias Lundquist", "Charlene Running Bear"], "companies": ["Black Hills Regional Heart & Vascular Hospital", "Pine Ridge Family Health Clinic", "Rapid City", "Indian Health Service", "Medicaid"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Black Hills Regional Heart & Vascular Hospital", "Pine Ridge Family Health Clinic", " Rapid City"], "health": ["myocardial infarction", "alcohol withdrawal", "type 2 diabetes", "tremor", "sweating", "agitation", "heart attack", "smoking", "Medicaid"], "sensitive": ["Oglala Sioux Tribe", "wife's death"], "names": ["Wendell", "Soraya", "Tobias", "Charlene"]}, "judged": {"candidates": 0, "requests": 0, "failures": 0, "places": [], "labels": {}}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 228.79999999701977, "modelMs": 0, "topicMs": 0, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "street", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "region", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 46, "text": "Black Hills Regional Heart & Vascular Hospital", "kind": "company", "source": "model", "canonical": "Black Hills Regional Heart & Vascular Hospital"}, {"start": 75, "end": 99, "text": "RUNNING BEAR, WENDELL K.